4. CONTINUITY OF LICENSE
------------------------------------

The licenses, permissions, rights, and obligations arising under this License
are intended to remain effective notwithstanding any transfer, succession,
change in ownership or control, or other event affecting a Right Holder,
Contributor, or holder of Rights in the Work or any Contribution. Except to
the extent that applicable law expressly provides otherwise, no such event
shall revoke, diminish, impair, suspend, or otherwise adversely affect any
license or permission previously granted to You under this License. Any
Successor shall be bound to honor grants previously made under this License,
and any statutory termination of such licenses or permissions shall have only
the effect expressly provided in this Section.

4.1 The Right Holder and each Contributor hereby promise that no transfer,
succession, death, dissolution, merger, acquisition, reorganization,
bankruptcy, insolvency proceeding, Change of Control, or other event
described in the definition of "Successor" shall diminish, suspend,
terminate, impair, or otherwise affect any license previously granted to
You.

4.2 No Successor or Contributor may unilaterally revoke, narrow, condition,
or impose additional restrictions on any license or permission previously
granted to You under Sections 2 and 3. The Right Holder and each Contributor
further agree that they shall not themselves take any action that would have
the effect of revoking, narrowing, conditioning, or imposing additional
restrictions on any such license or permission previously granted to You.
This Section 4 shall not be construed as an anti-assignment provision, and no
transfer described in the definition of "Successor" shall be deemed void,
invalid, or unenforceable by reason of any prohibition on assignment that
might otherwise apply under this License or applicable law.

4.3 The Right Holder and each Contributor hereby grant You the right to
refuse any request made by a Successor to alter, remove, or restate any
existing notice or any instruction or prescribed method of application stated
in Appendix A or Sections 5(b) and 5(c), whether in the Work or in any
Derivative Works that You received. The Right Holder and each Contributor
further agree that they shall not themselves require or compel You to make
any such alteration, removal, or restatement, and Your refusal to comply
with any such request shall not constitute a breach of this License.

4.4 Territorial Effect of Statutory Termination. If this License is terminated
by operation of a statutory right, and that statutory right arises under the
applicable law of a specific territory, such termination shall be effective
only with respect to that specific territory, and only where a Contributor has
invoked the applicable law of that specific territory. Such termination shall
not affect, and shall not be construed to affect, the validity,
effectiveness, or continuity of this License in any other territory.

4.5 Merger and Corporate Restructuring. For the avoidance of doubt, the term
"Successor" and the protections of this Section 4 apply regardless of the
legal form of the transaction, including a direct merger, forward merger,
forward triangular merger, or reverse triangular merger, and regardless of
whether the Right Holder, Contributor, or any Legal Entity holding Rights in
the Work is the surviving entity in such transaction. No characterization of
a transaction as not constituting an "assignment by operation of law" under
applicable corporate law shall be construed to remove that transaction from
the scope of this Section 4.


4.6 No Abandonment as Circumvention. A Successor's cessation of operations,
discontinuation of the Work, or reduction to a holding entity shall not, by
itself, be construed to terminate, suspend, or diminish any license granted
under this Section 4, nor shall it relieve a Successor of its obligations
under Sections 4.1 through 4.3.

